\strong{Batch Policy Gradient  Methods for  Improving Neural Conversation Models}

  \section{Abstract}

  We propose a new family of policy gradient methods for improving neural conversation models. Our methods are based on the idea of batching the gradient updates, which has been shown to be effective in other contexts. We show that our methods can be applied to a wide range of neural conversation models, including models that use recurrent neural networks, convolutional neural networks, and attention mechanisms. We also show that our methods can be applied to models that use a variety of training objectives, including maximum likelihood training, reinforcement learning, and adversarial training. We evaluate our methods on a variety of tasks, including dialogue generation, dialogue response selection, and dialogue policy learning. Our experiments show that our methods can improve the performance of neural conversation models on these tasks.

  \section{Keywords}

  Policy gradient methods, neural conversation models, batch gradient methods, reinforcement learning, adversarial training

